# Citation metadata for quantum-rat (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
# GitHub reads this file for its "Cite this repository" button.
# The second author entry is a placeholder: fill in the person to be credited
# (family-names, given-names and, if you have one, orcid), or delete it.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "quantum-rat: a deterministic embodied rat-brain simulator and lab console"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-03
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/PolyLabs-research/quantum-rat"
abstract: >-
  A deterministic, seeded simulator of a 2-D embodied point agent with a
  rat-inspired brain model, headless assays and tournaments, an analysis
  pipeline, and a local lab console for live runs and tick-by-tick replay.
  For a given seed, runs on the same platform reproduce the committed trace
  hashes bit for bit, which the test suite checks.
keywords:
  - simulation
  - hippocampal replay
  - spatial memory
  - determinism
  - embodied agent
authors:
